Momentum Theory


Significance
o Developed in 1865
o Uses simple Mass, Momentum and Energy balance, flow details not covered
o Easy ‘back of an envelop’ type of calculations
o Can predict hover and steady climb (no edgewise component)


Assumptions
o Rotor modeled as an actuator disk (no description of blades, number of blades, etc)
o The actuator disk adds momentum to the flow for generating force
o Flow is:
o Incompressible, Steady, Inviscid, Irrotational
o Flow is 1-Dimensional (totally uniform over the rotor disk)
o No Swirl


